\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0   Him alone possessing, He alone is mine
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 All my heart in Him confessing,
\par ne'er forgets His trust divine.
\par Naught I know of sadness,
\par Only of devotion, love and gladness
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  Him alone possessing, worldliness I  shun.
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Onward with my staff I'm pressing,
\par With my Lord the goal is won;
\par though' mankind, e'en Brother,
\par Walk the bright, broad way with one another.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par      3.  Him alone possessing, leave this worldly scene
\par         I have heaven's richest blessing,
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj this I've felt, have known and seen.
\par And my heart's devotion
\par can't be frightened by this world's commotion.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  Him alone processing, blessed in my sleep.
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 Thus my Lord, His love expressing,
\par Points the way for me to keep.
\par With His kind persuasion
\par \pard      I can overcome and gain salvation \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

